From: NeiroNext <mihail.rozshko@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:35:32 +0000
Subject: Forward ScreenSaver inhibitors to the session manager

light-locker owns org.freedesktop.ScreenSaver and kept the inhibitors
applications take there (VLC, Firefox while playing) to itself: they
stopped only its own activation. The session manager never heard of them,
so with the session's idle presence working, the session went idle,
blanked and locked during playback.

Each inhibitor is now also taken from org.gnome.SessionManager as an idle
inhibitor (flag 8, toplevel 0, the caller's application and reason, a
non-empty substitute when either is empty), asynchronously; the caller's
cookie and reply do not wait for it. It is released on UnInhibit and when
the caller's unique name goes away, also when that happens before the
session manager answered. Uninhibit goes to the unique name that gave the
cookie. When the session manager goes away its inhibitors are forgotten,
not taken again. Inhibitors held for light-locker go with its connection.
Cookies skip 0 and cookies in use.

A caller now counts as gone only when its own unique name goes away: a
live caller that takes or drops a well-known name keeps its inhibitors
(it used to lose them, light-locker's own included).

Nothing new is allowed: any client on the session bus can take a session
manager inhibitor itself. The application and reason become visible in the
session manager's inhibitor list on the same user's bus, as for any other
inhibitor. One session manager inhibitor per ScreenSaver inhibitor, gone
with its caller.

Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-13
